- The shelf: ready made things to put on the canvas, one gesture each.
- A person opening the editor is offered objects they recognise — a calculator, a
- map, the two of them already wired, a plain block — and not the several hundred
- classes a pack declares. Those are still here, one level down, because laying
- out the inside of a page needs the primitives of mol and nothing else will do.
$bog_vmap_app_shelf $mol_view
	- The palette field, held by the editor and passed through: the shelf shows what
	- the scene has actually loaded, so there is one value and not two.
	- Links separated by commas, stored exactly as typed. The first http(s) one is
	- the application whose objects join the shelf, the rest are lands of Giper Baza
	- holding component sources; anything else is refused and said so under the
	- field. One pack per frame, so a second address is refused by construction.
	links? \
	pack_link \
	land_classes /$mol_tree2
	- Names of every class the library holds — the pack and the lands on it —
	- handed in by the editor, which owns the one library of the session. Read
	- inside `Apps` and nowhere else: reading it fetches, and a dead address must
	- take down that one list rather than the panel around it.
	class_list /string
	- What the pointer is carrying, BY ITS ID, empty when nothing is being dragged,
	- and where the pointer is in viewport coordinates. The same protocol the
	- palette has always spoken, and now spoken in one place: a class row of the
	- second level writes its class name here through the binding below, a shelf row
	- writes the id of its item, and the id tells the two apart because a class name
	- starts with a dollar and an item id never does.
	dragged? \
	drag_x? 0
	drag_y? 0
	- Id of an item asked for by a plain click, which the editor answers by putting
	- it in the middle of the canvas. A press that turns into a drag never becomes a
	- click, so the two gestures do not fight.
	place? \
	- Files picked in the dialog. Written by the button, answered empty: this is an
	- event carrying a payload, not a list the panel keeps.
	files? /File
	classes_showed? false
	sub <= body /$mol_view
	-
	Title $mol_view
		sub /
			\Полка
	-
	- Everything above the second level scrolls as one: on a short window twelve
	- items, the address field, the button and the objects of an application do not
	- fit, and without a scroll of its own the panel pushed the whole page down and
	- took the head bar off the screen with it.
	-
	- `$mol_scroll` lays every child into the same cell, so it holds exactly ONE
	- node and the stack goes inside that one.
	Stack $mol_scroll
		sub /
			<= Stack_body $mol_view
				sub <= stack_content /$mol_view
	-
	Items $mol_list
		rows <= item_rows /
	-
	- Where an application comes from. Outside `Apps` on purpose: a mistyped address
	- must leave the field it was typed into reachable, and the list is exactly what
	- a bad address takes down.
	Source $mol_view
		sub <= source_content /$mol_view
	-
	Links $mol_string
		hint \Адрес приложения, ленды через запятую
		value? <=> links?
	-
	- Files of a mol module brought straight from the disk. What they carry goes
	- into the component library of the user, whose link joins the field above, so
	- from that moment on it is the same library another scene would be handed.
	Import $mol_view
		sub /
			<= Import_open $mol_button_open
				hint \Файлы .view.tree модуля mol. Объявления приедут, поведение — нет
				accept \.tree
				multiple true
				files? <=> files?
			<= Import_title $mol_view
				sub /
					\Файлы модуля
	-
	- Which files were not taken, and why. Rendered only while there is something
	- to say, like the refusals of the field above it.
	Import_note $mol_view
		sub / <= import_note? \
	-
	- CRUD over the library of the user. The same store the publish button holds:
	- both write into the one library the home land points at, and both find it
	- through the same list of pointers.
	Store $bog_vmap_app_publish_store
	-
	- What was typed and not taken, and why, right under the field. Rendered only
	- while there is something to say: a second pack is refused by construction and
	- a person who typed one has to learn that from the screen, not from a log.
	Note $mol_view
		sub / <= rejected_note \
	-
	- Objects of the connected application: every class it declares that is not
	- part of mol itself. A deployed mol application is a library of components
	- already, so this needs nothing of the application's author.
	Apps $mol_view
		sub <= apps_content /$mol_view
	-
	Apps_head $mol_view
		sub /
			<= apps_title \
	-
	App_list $mol_list
		rows <= app_rows /
	-
	- Why an address brought nothing. In place of the list and not beside it: there
	- is nothing to list, and a dead address is the whole content of the section
	- until it is fixed.
	Apps_note $mol_view
		sub / <= app_error \
	-
	- The second level, folded away by default. A check and not an expander: the
	- palette has to GROW into whatever the shelf left, and inside an expander it
	- would sit in a list that sizes itself by its content, so the class list would
	- have no height to scroll in.
	Level $mol_check
		title \Все классы пака
		hint \Классы донорского пака целиком: примитивы, из которых верстают внутри блока
		checked? <=> classes_showed?
	-
	- The old palette, demoted to a second level. Rendered only while it is open,
	- so a folded panel does not fetch a pack tree it is not showing.
	Palette $bog_vmap_app_palette
		compact true
		pack_link <= pack_link
		land_classes <= land_classes
		dragged? <=> dragged?
		drag_x? <=> drag_x?
		drag_y? <=> drag_y?
	-
	- One row per item. The same row the palette uses: a line of text that starts
	- carrying its item on `pointerdown`, because the native drag protocol cannot be
	- driven by synthetic events and would hand the drop to the browser.
	Item_row* $bog_vmap_app_palette_item
		title <= item_title* \
		hint <= item_hint* \
		click? <=> item_click*? null
		drag_start? <=> item_drag*? null
